#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# acsc

#% text
# `acsc(z)` gives the inverse cosecant.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For complex `z` the principal value is `asin(1/z)`.

#% item
# Exact special values and odd symmetry are applied; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
acsc(2)
#% output
#= (1/6)*pi

#% cell
acsc(3.0)
#% output
#= 0.3398369094541219

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
acsc(-x)
#% output
#= -acsc(x)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(acsc(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= 1.570796326794896619231321691639751 - 1.7627471740390860504652186499595846im

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `atan`, `asin`, `acos`
